588
00:25:42,840 --> 00:25:50,630
So whether you work in an office, work remotely, or want to prepare for an international company someday, this lesson is perfect for you.

589
00:25:51,030 --> 00:25:51,450
All right.

590
00:25:51,840 --> 00:25:54,000
Let's jump into our first business phrase.

591
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:57,660
Our first phrase is, let's get the ball rolling.

592
00:25:57,640 --> 00:26:03,210
This phrase means, let's start something, usually a project, meeting, or discussion.

593
00:26:03,610 --> 00:26:07,640
Everyone is here now, so let's get the ball rolling.

594
00:26:08,020 --> 00:26:08,480
Sounds good.

595
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:10,940
I'll begin with today's agenda.

596
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:12,630
Very natural meeting English.

597
00:26:13,850 --> 00:26:15,290
Here's another useful phrase.

598
00:26:15,890 --> 00:26:17,190
I'm tied up at the moment.

599
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:19,700
This means that you're very busy right now.

600
00:26:20,180 --> 00:26:21,540
Example conversation.

601
00:26:21,840 --> 00:26:23,990
Can you help me review this report right now?

602
00:26:24,530 --> 00:26:27,330
I'm tied up at the moment, but I can help you after lunch.

603
00:26:27,760 --> 00:26:28,400
No problem.

604
00:26:28,820 --> 00:26:32,760
This phrase sounds much more natural than simply saying, I'm busy.

605
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:33,850
Exactly.

606
00:26:33,890 --> 00:26:36,690
Next phrase, we're on the same page.

607
00:26:37,130 --> 00:26:40,340
This means everyone understands and agrees about something.

608
00:26:40,760 --> 00:26:42,380
Example conversation.

609
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:47,590
Before we contact the client, I want to make sure we're on the same page about the pricing strategy.

610
00:26:48,010 --> 00:26:48,570
Absolutely.

611
00:26:48,950 --> 00:26:52,380
We'll offer the premium package with free support for six months.

612
00:26:52,800 --> 00:26:53,260
Perfect.

613
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:55,530
Great business communication phrase.

614
00:26:55,890 --> 00:26:57,790
Here's another practical expression.

615
00:26:57,770 --> 00:26:59,290
Let's touch base later.

616
00:26:59,710 --> 00:27:01,860
This means let's communicate later.

617
00:27:02,340 --> 00:27:03,460
Example conversation.

618
00:27:04,180 --> 00:27:06,680
I still need more information from the finance team.

619
00:27:07,040 --> 00:27:07,360
All right.

620
00:27:07,770 --> 00:27:11,110
Let's touch base later this afternoon after you receive the numbers.

621
00:27:11,610 --> 00:27:12,210
Sounds good.

622
00:27:12,670 --> 00:27:14,390
Very common office English.

623
00:27:14,380 --> 00:27:16,540
Especially in American workplaces.

624
00:27:17,040 --> 00:27:19,300
Next phrase, I'll keep you posted.

625
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:23,210
This means I'll continue updating you about the situation.

626
00:27:23,630 --> 00:27:24,730
Example conversation.

627
00:27:25,150 --> 00:27:27,360
Has the client made a final decision yet?

628
00:27:27,740 --> 00:27:31,020
Not yet, but I'll keep you posted as soon as I hear anything.

629
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:31,960
Thanks.

630
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:35,140
Very useful phrase for teamwork and project updates.

631
00:27:35,710 --> 00:27:36,330
Absolutely.

632
00:27:36,370 --> 00:27:38,130
Here's another great expression.

633
00:27:38,450 --> 00:27:40,550
We need to think outside the box.

634
00:27:41,050 --> 00:27:43,810
This means thinking creatively or differently.

635
00:27:43,850 --> 00:27:45,360
Example conversation.

636
00:27:45,860 --> 00:27:48,240
Sales have been dropping for three months now.

637
00:27:48,700 --> 00:27:53,460
Then we need to think outside the box and try a completely new marketing strategy.

638
00:27:53,940 --> 00:27:54,380
I agree.

639
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:57,150
Excellent phrase for brainstorming sessions.

640
00:27:57,570 --> 00:27:58,390
Definitely.

641
00:27:58,370 --> 00:28:01,790
Next phrase is, that's a win-win situation.

642
00:28:02,290 --> 00:28:04,780
This means both sides benefit from something.

643
00:28:05,220 --> 00:28:06,300
Example conversation.

644
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:12,270
If we extend the contract, the client gets a discount and we secure long-term business.

645
00:28:12,670 --> 00:28:13,250
Exactly.

646
00:28:13,510 --> 00:28:15,850
It's a win-win situation for everyone.

647
00:28:15,830 --> 00:28:17,640
Very professional expression.

648
00:28:18,080 --> 00:28:20,840
And extremely common in negotiations.

649
00:28:20,860 --> 00:28:23,200
Next phrase, let's cut to the chase.

650
00:28:23,690 --> 00:28:27,590
This means getting directly to the important point without wasting time.

651
00:28:28,030 --> 00:28:29,170
Example conversation.

652
00:28:29,820 --> 00:28:32,020
We only have 20 minutes left in this meeting.

653
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:36,310
Then let's cut to the chase and discuss the budget issue immediately.

654
00:28:36,290 --> 00:28:36,790
Agreed.

655
00:28:37,190 --> 00:28:39,170
Great expression for busy workplaces.

656
00:28:39,590 --> 00:28:40,190
Definitely.

657
00:28:40,580 --> 00:28:42,460
Here's another practical business phrase.

658
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:43,900
I'll take care of it.

659
00:28:44,300 --> 00:28:47,270
This means I'll handle the task or problem.

660
00:28:47,670 --> 00:28:48,730
Example conversation.

661
00:28:49,170 --> 00:28:52,220
The conference room still isn't ready for the client meeting.

662
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:54,400
Don't worry, I'll take care of it right away.

663
00:28:54,840 --> 00:28:55,240
Thank you.

664
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:58,030
Short, confident, and professional.

665
00:28:58,410 --> 00:28:58,970
Exactly.

666
00:28:59,450 --> 00:29:02,330
Next phrase, we need to prioritize this.

667
00:29:02,810 --> 00:29:07,240
Prioritize means deciding something is more important than other tasks.

668
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:09,360
Example conversation.

669
00:29:09,340 --> 00:29:12,210
The customer complained about a serious payment issue.

670
00:29:12,630 --> 00:29:16,240
Then we need to prioritize this before working on anything else.

671
00:29:16,820 --> 00:29:17,460
Absolutely.

672
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:19,880
Very important business vocabulary.

673
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:21,810
Here's another useful expression.

674
00:29:22,350 --> 00:29:23,170
I'm looking into it.

675
00:29:23,650 --> 00:29:26,560
This means you're investigating or checking something.

676
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:28,040
Example conversation.

677
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:30,530
Do we know why the shipment was delayed?

678
00:29:30,670 --> 00:29:32,940
Not yet, but I'm looking into it now.

679
00:29:33,360 --> 00:29:34,620
Okay, keep me updated.

680
00:29:35,020 --> 00:29:37,330
Great phrase for professional communication.

681
00:29:37,730 --> 00:29:38,330
Definitely.

682
00:29:38,730 --> 00:29:41,380
Next phrase, let's circle back tomorrow.

683
00:29:41,840 --> 00:29:44,310
This means discussing something again later.

684
00:29:44,350 --> 00:29:45,850
Example conversation.

685
00:29:46,290 --> 00:29:48,620
We still don't have all the information we need.

686
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:52,810
Then let's circle back tomorrow after the finance team sends the report.

687
00:29:53,230 --> 00:29:54,030
Sounds like a plan.

688
00:29:54,530 --> 00:29:56,120
Very modern office English.

689
00:29:56,560 --> 00:29:58,940
You hear this phrase constantly in meetings.

690
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:00,900
Here's another important phrase.

691
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:03,130
We're running behind schedule.

692
00:30:03,530 --> 00:30:05,850
This means the work is slower than planned.

693
00:30:06,290 --> 00:30:07,430
Example conversation.

694
00:30:07,490 --> 00:30:11,380
The website redesign should have been finished last week.

695
00:30:11,490 --> 00:30:12,040
I know.

696
00:30:12,100 --> 00:30:16,200
Unfortunately, we're running behind schedule because of technical problems.

697
00:30:16,620 --> 00:30:17,630
That's frustrating.

698
00:30:18,130 --> 00:30:19,970
Very realistic workplace English.

699
00:30:20,490 --> 00:30:21,130
Absolutely.

700
00:30:21,570 --> 00:30:24,680
Next phrase is, let's brainstorm some ideas.

701
00:30:25,160 --> 00:30:28,460
Brainstorm means discussing creative ideas together.

702
00:30:28,870 --> 00:30:29,970
Example conversation.

703
00:30:30,370 --> 00:30:33,230
We need a better way to attract younger customers.

704
00:30:33,350 --> 00:30:33,890
Agreed.

705
00:30:34,250 --> 00:30:36,990
Let's brainstorm some ideas during tomorrow's meeting.

706
00:30:37,410 --> 00:30:37,790
Perfect.

707
00:30:38,250 --> 00:30:39,780
Excellent collaboration phrase.

708
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:40,780
Definitely.

709
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:42,900
Here's another natural expression.

710
00:30:43,520 --> 00:30:45,560
I completely understand your concern.

711
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:49,190
This means you understand someone's worry or problem.

712
00:30:49,610 --> 00:30:50,750
Example conversation.

713
00:30:51,390 --> 00:30:54,170
I'm worried the deadline is too short for our team.

714
00:30:54,710 --> 00:30:59,760
I completely understand your concern, and we'll discuss possible solutions together.

715
00:30:59,740 --> 00:31:00,320
Thank you.

716
00:31:00,720 --> 00:31:02,960
Great phrase for managers and team leaders.

717
00:31:03,500 --> 00:31:05,450
Very professional and respectful.

718
00:31:05,890 --> 00:31:08,870
Next phrase is, we need to stay on track.

719
00:31:09,330 --> 00:31:12,630
This means continuing to make progress towards the goal.

720
00:31:13,050 --> 00:31:14,130
Example conversation.

721
00:31:14,620 --> 00:31:16,640
Should we postpone the presentation again?

722
00:31:16,680 --> 00:31:21,140
No, we need to stay on track if we want to finish the project on time.

723
00:31:21,540 --> 00:31:21,980
You're right.

724
00:31:22,460 --> 00:31:25,010
Excellent phrase for productivity discussions.

725
00:31:24,980 --> 00:31:25,890
Absolutely.

726
00:31:26,310 --> 00:31:28,090
Here's another useful business phrase.

727
00:31:28,630 --> 00:31:29,640
Let me double check.

728
00:31:30,100 --> 00:31:32,770
This means checking something again carefully.

729
00:31:33,230 --> 00:31:34,330
Example conversation.

730
00:31:34,850 --> 00:31:37,060
Are you sure the meeting starts at 10 a.m.?

731
00:31:37,500 --> 00:31:39,370
Let me double check the schedule quickly.

732
00:31:39,830 --> 00:31:40,330
Okay.

733
00:31:40,310 --> 00:31:42,050
Very common office phrase.

734
00:31:42,510 --> 00:31:43,960
And very practical, too.

735
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:48,110
Next phrase is, we should avoid unnecessary risks.

736
00:31:48,590 --> 00:31:51,680
This means being careful and preventing problems.

737
00:31:52,180 --> 00:31:53,220
Example conversation.

738
00:31:53,660 --> 00:31:56,510
Should we launch the product before final testing?

739
00:31:56,490 --> 00:32:01,500
No, we should avoid unnecessary risks and wait until testing is complete.

740
00:32:01,940 --> 00:32:02,880
I agree completely.

741
00:32:03,440 --> 00:32:04,680
Smart business language.

742
00:32:05,080 --> 00:32:05,680
Definitely.

743
00:32:06,060 --> 00:32:07,210
Here's another expression.

744
00:32:07,730 --> 00:32:08,990
Thanks for bringing this up.

745
00:32:09,450 --> 00:32:13,010
This means thanking someone for mentioning an issue or idea.

746
00:32:13,430 --> 00:32:14,500
Example conversation.

747
00:32:15,040 --> 00:32:19,020
I think our customer support response time is becoming too slow.

748
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,350
Thanks for bringing this up.

749
00:32:20,610 --> 00:32:22,670
We definitely need to improve that area.

750
00:32:23,010 --> 00:32:23,750
Glad you agree.

751
00:32:24,290 --> 00:32:25,740
Very useful during meetings.

752
00:32:26,300 --> 00:32:26,940
Absolutely.

753
00:32:27,340 --> 00:32:30,090
Next phrase is, we're making good progress.

754
00:32:30,530 --> 00:32:33,130
This means the work is improving successfully.

755
00:32:33,150 --> 00:32:34,580
Example conversation.

756
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:37,280
How's the new software project going?

757
00:32:37,260 --> 00:32:41,090
We're making good progress and should finish testing next week.

758
00:32:41,110 --> 00:32:41,750
Excellent news.

759
00:32:42,190 --> 00:32:44,420
Positive and motivating business English.

760
00:32:44,800 --> 00:32:45,380
Definitely.

761
00:32:45,420 --> 00:32:47,260
Here's another important phrase.

762
00:32:47,820 --> 00:32:49,290
I'd appreciate your feedback.

763
00:32:49,770 --> 00:32:52,910
This means you want someone's opinion or suggestions.

764
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:54,460
Example conversation.

765
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:57,570
I finished the first draft of the presentation.

766
00:32:57,550 --> 00:33:01,490
Great, I'd appreciate your feedback before we show it to the client.

767
00:33:01,910 --> 00:33:03,570
Sure, I'll review it this afternoon.

768
00:33:04,110 --> 00:33:05,800
Very professional communication.

769
00:33:06,280 --> 00:33:07,520
And very polite, too.

770
00:33:08,100 --> 00:33:10,820
Next phrase, we need a backup plan.

771
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:15,170
A backup plan means an alternative plan in case something fails.

772
00:33:15,670 --> 00:33:17,390
Example conversation.

773
00:33:17,370 --> 00:33:20,620
What if the system crashes during the presentation tomorrow?

774
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:23,400
Then we'll need a backup plan just in case.

775
00:33:23,920 --> 00:33:24,660
Smart thinking.

776
00:33:25,120 --> 00:33:26,570
Important business expression.

777
00:33:26,950 --> 00:33:27,530
Definitely.

778
00:33:27,910 --> 00:33:29,390
Here's another practical phrase.

779
00:33:29,850 --> 00:33:31,380
Let's keep the momentum going.

780
00:33:31,820 --> 00:33:34,980
This means continuing strong progress and energy.

781
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:36,500
Example conversation.

782
00:33:36,980 --> 00:33:39,770
Sales increased significantly this quarter.

783
00:33:39,750 --> 00:33:40,950
That's fantastic.

784
00:33:41,370 --> 00:33:43,670
Let's keep the momentum going next month, too.

785
00:33:44,190 --> 00:33:44,780
Absolutely.

786
00:33:45,150 --> 00:33:47,080
Great motivational language.

787
00:33:47,100 --> 00:33:49,320
Very common in leadership conversations.

788
00:33:49,820 --> 00:33:53,160
Next phrase is, I think we're heading in the right direction.

789
00:33:53,620 --> 00:33:56,790
This means progress seems positive and successful.

790
00:33:57,210 --> 00:33:58,270
Example conversation.

791
00:33:58,730 --> 00:34:01,750
Customer satisfaction scores improved again this month.

792
00:34:02,270 --> 00:34:02,730
Excellent.

793
00:34:03,210 --> 00:34:05,220
I think we're heading in the right direction.

794
00:34:05,200 --> 00:34:05,820
I agree.

795
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:08,420
Positive and encouraging business English.

796
00:34:08,820 --> 00:34:09,400
Definitely.

797
00:34:09,860 --> 00:34:10,160
Wow.

