We're not just going to list phrases.

815
00:35:21,940 --> 00:35:29,110
We'll show you meaning, context, and real conversations so you understand how to use them in actual work situations.

816
00:35:29,770 --> 00:35:30,270
Let's begin.

817
00:35:30,330 --> 00:35:33,030
Let's start with a very common phrase.

818
00:35:33,570 --> 00:35:34,550
Let's touch base.

819
00:35:35,230 --> 00:35:35,550
Meaning.

820
00:35:36,110 --> 00:35:40,520
This means to briefly connect or check in with someone about a task or project.

821
00:35:41,200 --> 00:35:42,600
Example usage.

822
00:35:42,620 --> 00:35:49,390
Instead of saying, we should talk later, you can say, let's touch base later this afternoon on the client report.

823
00:35:49,750 --> 00:35:51,340
In a real office conversation.

824
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:53,060
Hey, are you free now?

825
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:55,940
I just wanted to touch base on the presentation slides.

826
00:35:56,560 --> 00:35:59,040
Sure, give me five minutes and we'll go through it together.

827
00:35:59,740 --> 00:36:01,570
Next phrase, I'm looped in.

828
00:36:01,610 --> 00:36:07,110
Meaning, this means you are included in communication or updates about a project.

829
00:36:07,850 --> 00:36:12,100
Example usage, please make sure I'm looped in on all client emails.

830
00:36:12,760 --> 00:36:16,500
Conversation example, are you aware of the budget changes?

831
00:36:16,620 --> 00:36:20,260
Yes, I'm already looped in by the finance team, so I've seen the updates.

832
00:36:20,990 --> 00:36:23,750
Another important phrase, let's circle back.

833
00:36:24,390 --> 00:36:26,750
Meaning, to return to a topic later.

834
00:36:26,790 --> 00:36:31,440
Example usage, let's circle back to this after we get more data.

835
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:35,310
Real conversation, what do you think about the new proposal?

836
00:36:36,050 --> 00:36:37,570
I think it needs more analysis.

837
00:36:37,870 --> 00:36:40,330
Let's circle back tomorrow after reviewing the numbers.

838
00:36:41,070 --> 00:36:42,980
Next phrase, I'm swamped.

839
00:36:43,680 --> 00:36:46,220
Meaning, you are very busy with work.

840
00:36:46,490 --> 00:36:50,110
Example usage, I can't take on extra tasks this week.

841
00:36:50,330 --> 00:36:50,890
I'm swamped.

842
00:36:51,530 --> 00:36:54,560
Conversation example, can you help me with this report?

843
00:36:55,220 --> 00:36:57,420
I'd love to help, but I'm swamped right now.

844
00:36:57,600 --> 00:36:59,680
Can we do it after 4 p.m.?

845
00:36:59,700 --> 00:37:03,230
Let's move to another useful phrase, on the same page.

846
00:37:03,890 --> 00:37:07,530
Meaning, everyone understands and agrees on the same idea.

847
00:37:08,230 --> 00:37:13,120
Example usage, just to confirm, we're targeting Friday for the launch, right?

848
00:37:13,540 --> 00:37:15,140
Yes, we're on the same page.

849
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:16,860
Friday is the final deadline.

850
00:37:17,580 --> 00:37:19,730
Next phrase, take it offline.

851
00:37:20,350 --> 00:37:24,530
Meaning, to continue a discussion privately or outside the meeting.

852
00:37:25,280 --> 00:37:27,700
Example usage, this issue is detailed.

853
00:37:27,940 --> 00:37:28,960
Let's take it offline.

854
00:37:29,520 --> 00:37:33,230
Real conversation, I think this topic needs more discussion.

855
00:37:33,930 --> 00:37:36,210
Agreed, let's take it offline after the meeting.

856
00:37:36,890 --> 00:37:39,800
Now a very useful phrase, action item.

857
00:37:40,120 --> 00:37:43,860
Meaning, a specific task that needs to be done after a meeting.

858
00:37:44,620 --> 00:37:48,220
Example usage, let's assign action items before we finish.

859
00:37:48,930 --> 00:37:51,350
So, what are the action items from today's meeting?

860
00:37:52,050 --> 00:37:55,470
I'll handle the client email, and you'll prepare the financial summary.

861
00:37:56,130 --> 00:37:58,010
Another key phrase, follow up.

862
00:37:58,670 --> 00:38:02,380
Meaning, to check progress or continue communication about something.

863
00:38:02,980 --> 00:38:06,540
Example usage, I will follow up with the supplier tomorrow.

864
00:38:07,200 --> 00:38:10,010
Conversation example, did the client respond?

865
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:12,890
Not yet, but I'll follow up with them this afternoon.

866
00:38:12,930 --> 00:38:15,510
Next phrase, keep me posted.

867
00:38:16,190 --> 00:38:18,030
Meaning, to keep someone updated.

868
00:38:18,770 --> 00:38:22,060
Example usage, keep me posted on the project progress.

869
00:38:22,780 --> 00:38:24,580
So, I'm meeting the client tomorrow.

870
00:38:25,220 --> 00:38:27,910
Great, keep me posted if they request any changes.

871
00:38:28,590 --> 00:38:30,370
Now let's talk about backlog.

872
00:38:31,050 --> 00:38:34,100
Meaning, work or tasks that are still unfinished.

873
00:38:34,740 --> 00:38:38,200
Example usage, we need to clear the backlog this week.

874
00:38:38,520 --> 00:38:39,560
Conversation example.

875
00:38:40,260 --> 00:38:41,560
Why are we behind schedule?

876
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:45,270
We still have a backlog of pending approvals from last week.

877
00:38:45,990 --> 00:38:48,730
Another important phrase, to get up to speed.

878
00:38:49,430 --> 00:38:52,470
Meaning, to quickly learn or understand something new.

879
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:54,080
Example usage.

880
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:57,400
It will take me a day to get up to speed with this project.

881
00:38:58,080 --> 00:39:00,220
So, how are you finding the new system?

882
00:39:00,900 --> 00:39:01,320
It's good.

883
00:39:01,660 --> 00:39:03,610
I just need a little time to get up to speed.

884
00:39:04,310 --> 00:39:05,930
Now moving to bandwidth.

885
00:39:06,300 --> 00:39:09,700
Meaning your capacity or availability to take on work.

886
00:39:10,460 --> 00:39:14,660
Example usage, I don't have the bandwidth to take on new tasks right now.

887
00:39:15,330 --> 00:39:17,290
Can you lead another project this month?

888
00:39:18,050 --> 00:39:19,990
Sorry, I don't have the bandwidth right now.

889
00:39:20,710 --> 00:39:23,330
Another useful phrase, raise a concern.

890
00:39:24,010 --> 00:39:27,340
Meaning to bring up a problem or issue professionally.

891
00:39:28,120 --> 00:39:32,380
Example usage, I'd like to raise a concern about the timeline.

892
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:33,820
Everything okay with the project?

893
00:39:34,260 --> 00:39:37,640
Yes, but I need to raise a concern about resource allocation.

894
00:39:38,280 --> 00:39:40,490
Now let's talk about value added.

895
00:39:41,270 --> 00:39:44,310
Meaning, something that improves quality or benefit.

896
00:39:44,950 --> 00:39:48,640
Example usage, this feature is value added for customers.

897
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:52,720
Example conversation, why should we include this service?

898
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:56,650
Because it's value added and increases customer satisfaction.

899
00:39:57,390 --> 00:39:59,510
Another phrase, end to end.

900
00:40:00,250 --> 00:40:03,140
Meaning, from start to finish of a process.

901
00:40:03,470 --> 00:40:06,800
Example usage, we manage the project end-to-end.

902
00:40:07,540 --> 00:40:09,700
So who is responsible for this process?

903
00:40:10,460 --> 00:40:13,610
Our team handles it end-to-end from planning to delivery.

904
00:40:14,290 --> 00:40:17,680
Now a very practical phrase, let's prioritize this.

905
00:40:18,420 --> 00:40:20,840
Meaning to treat something as most important.

906
00:40:21,700 --> 00:40:25,770
Example usage, let's prioritize urgent client requests first.

907
00:40:26,510 --> 00:40:28,950
So we have multiple tasks pending.

908
00:40:29,290 --> 00:40:32,890
Let's prioritize the client issue before anything else.

909
00:40:32,910 --> 00:40:35,280
Another important phrase, we're aligned.

910
00:40:35,960 --> 00:40:39,020
Meaning everyone agrees and understands the direction.

911
00:40:39,800 --> 00:40:43,270
Example usage, we're aligned on the strategy moving forward.

912
00:40:43,970 --> 00:40:46,250
So we proceed with the new marketing plan.

913
00:40:46,970 --> 00:40:48,160
Yes, we're aligned on it.

914
00:40:48,840 --> 00:40:50,820
Let's end with one final phrase.

915
00:40:51,400 --> 00:40:52,760
Let's take this forward.

916
00:40:53,440 --> 00:40:56,970
Meaning to continue developing or progressing an idea.

917
00:40:57,270 --> 00:40:58,150
Example usage.

918
00:40:58,690 --> 00:40:59,990
This is a strong proposal.

919
00:41:00,250 --> 00:41:01,090
Let's take it forward.

920
00:41:01,770 --> 00:41:02,790
Conversation example.

921
00:41:03,490 --> 00:41:05,120
I think this idea has potential.

922
00:41:05,780 --> 00:41:06,180
I agree.

923
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:08,100
Let's take this forward in the next meeting.

924
00:41:08,780 --> 00:41:13,690
That brings us to the end of today's session on real business English phrases for daily work.

925
00:41:14,290 --> 00:41:17,670
Remember, fluency is not about using complicated words.

926
00:41:18,110 --> 00:41:21,760
It's about using the right phrases naturally in the right situations.

927
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:26,160
Practice these in your workplace conversations, emails, and meetings.

928
00:41:26,510 --> 00:41:39,000
Thank you for joining us today, and we'll see you in the next episode.
